  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39835994",
      "title": "Dynamic & Conditional Inline Styles",
      "sourceHash": "63c7e280c5d3064190d58faefbab2ce2c890d9de3b42783d97a61149fe914468",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "So let's stick to inline styling for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "though I will remove the inline styles from this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 10.563,
          "en": "because I don't really need them here anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "But let's now switch to AuthInputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "and there let's say we wanna conditionally style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 24.03,
          "en": "those inputs if they are invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.03,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "And I am actually already doing this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 30.21,
          "en": "by conditionally adding a class name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.21,
          "end": 32.493,
          "en": "And I'll get back to this in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 34.83,
          "en": "For the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.83,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "let's comment out this line of code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.53,
          "end": 41.55,
          "en": "on both inputs and let's instead try to achieve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.55,
          "end": 43.143,
          "en": "by adding inline styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 48.34,
          "en": "Now first, let's take a look at the index.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "and there at these invalid classes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 57.56,
          "en": "which are responsible for applying some invalid styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 61.38,
          "en": "And let's now try to set this background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "So this reddish color here with inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 68.853,
          "en": "on this input here if it happens to be invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 73.443,
          "en": "For that, of course, we can set background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.31,
          "end": 77.1,
          "en": "And now setting a value conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "so dynamically in the end, is pretty simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "We just have to check what our condition is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "and in this case, it's this emailNotValid constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "which contains true or false depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 91.923,
          "en": "on the result of this code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 95.463,
          "en": "So depending on this condition here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "And we can therefore then just use emailNotValid here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "in a turnary expression to set the background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "that should be applied if this is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 110.193,
          "en": "So if the email address is not valid here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 114.66,
          "en": "and to define the color that should be applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.66,
          "end": 116.31,
          "en": "if this is not true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.31,
          "end": 118.233,
          "en": "So if the email is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "So here, if email is not valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.84,
          "en": "I wanna apply this reddish color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.84,
          "end": 127.23,
          "en": "otherwise I wanna apply my default background color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.23,
          "end": 129.663,
          "en": "which is this background color here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 132.693,
          "en": "this light grayish color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 136.23,
          "en": "And that's therefore, the value we wanna use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 139.023,
          "en": "in the else part of the turnary expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.64,
          "end": 142.07999999999998,
          "en": "And that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 144.243,
          "en": "If we now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "you'll see that if I click sign in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "this input here gets highlighted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "with a light red color thanks to my conditional styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 157.29,
          "en": "And this, of course, becomes even clearer if I use just red",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.29,
          "end": 160.713,
          "en": "as a temporary value here, because now it's really red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.03300000000002,
          "en": "So let's switch back to the other approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 169.07999999999998,
          "en": "And that's therefore how you can add dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "and conditional styles when using inline styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 174.72,
          "en": "And we could, of course, also do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.72,
          "end": 179.72,
          "en": "on the password input here, but I'm not going to do it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.39,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "because the disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 185.61,
          "en": "with inline styling still is that you often end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.61,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "with a lot of duplication and that all your CSS code goes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 193.203,
          "en": "into the JSX code, which also isn't ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.4,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "And therefore, as a next step, let's take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 199.38,
          "en": "at this class name here and let's see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "how we can conditionally style elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 205.203,
          "en": "when using vanilla CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
